{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe spell of fair weather is broken. The air in Vienna has turned heavy and grey, and with it, the Kleins have departed. We did little more than share meals during their brief stay, but it was pleasant to have company while the sun still shone. I have decided to remain a few more days. There are corners of this city I have not yet walked, and now that the rain has come, I can see them better through the quiet.\n\nI am not in a hurry to return to Berlin. The journey is slow, which suits me. I hope you and the boys are well. Tell Karl to keep his studies steady; do not let him slacken now that I am away. I will write again when I have settled into my next inn.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080378,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":174,"prompt_tokens":920,"total_tokens":1094,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Z9oWKyy6SoqoaFOcSmgfaIHfQDSVYiiR","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":920,"prompt_ms":939.205,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.020875,"prompt_per_second":979.5518550263254,"predicted_n":174,"predicted_ms":4218.904,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.386728323699426,"predicted_per_second":41.00591053979896}}